\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Which fine families approach a tower?}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{The massive family of \ref{fdip-01CK} is already compatible
at every depth. A different sequence of fine precisions need not
have this exact compatibility; it can still approach the same
Gaussian law when observed at a fixed coarse depth. The single-step
calculation in \ref{fdip-01CL} follows each retained coefficient
through blocking. What convergence of these coefficients is both
necessary and sufficient to approach a prescribed tower at every
fixed depth?}
